#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# replace

#% text
# `replace(x, rules)` applies the first rule whose left side matches the whole of `x`, and gives `x` itself when none does.

#% text
# `replace(x, rules, levels)` applies the rules to each part of `x` at the levels, inner parts first.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `rules` is one rule `p -> r` or a list of rules; the result of a rule is evaluated.

#% item
# `rewrite` (`/.`) tries every part from the outside in; `replace` only the whole term or the levels given.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
replace(x^2, x^2 -> y)
#% output
#= y

#% cell
replace([x^2], x^2 -> y)
#% output
#= [x^2]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# At level 1 only:

#% cell
replace([x^2, [x^2]], x^2 -> y, [1])
#% output
#= [y, [x^2]]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `rewrite` reaches every part:

#% cell
rewrite([x^2, [x^2]], x^2 -> y)
#% output
#= [y, [y]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `rewrite`, `replace_part`, `cases`
